    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0933" n="921" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg921"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114 Mail/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-31">August 31,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received August 31—2:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5379. American interests Japan. Department’s 1067 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >1967</hi>], August 16.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d774-f1"/> Swiss
                    representative, Tokyo, informs Legation Japanese Minister Foreign Affairs<anchor
                        n="16" xml:id="d774-f2"/> states he would take necessary measures transmit
                    next exchange vessel correspondence of POW’s, civilian internees as well as
                    25-word messages from American citizens Far East. Japanese Government expects
                    reciprocal treatment and requests confirmation that American Government will
                    transmit next exchange vessel communications of types mentioned from Japanese in
                    United States.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d774-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Gaimusho<anchor n="18" xml:id="d774-f4"/> communicated identical proposal British
                    Government concerning British subjects Far East.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d774-f1" n="15" xml:id="d774-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d774-f2" n="16" xml:id="d774-f2-content">
                <p>Mamoru Shigemitsu.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d774-f3" n="17" xml:id="d774-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 2152, September 2, to the Minister in Switzerland, the Department
                    stated it was “giving correspondence from Japanese in United States reciprocal
                    treatment as requested.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d774-f4" n="18" xml:id="d774-f4-content">
                <p>Japanese Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
